IMPORT prelude

-- Minnesota Statutes, chapter 142G (Minnesota Family Investment Program, MFIP, Minnesota's TANF cash and food assistance),
-- with the chapter 256P rules it applies, and the Transitional Standard the commissioner published for October 1, 2026.
-- The assistance unit (142G.17, subds. 1, 3); the property limit (256P.02, subd. 2); the 60-month limit (142G.40, subds. 1,
-- 4(a)); the initial income test (142G.16, subd. 1); the assistance payment (142G.16, subd. 2; 142G.17, subds. 5, 7) with
-- the earned income disregard (256P.03), the $50 rental-subsidy rule (142G.31, subd. 6) and the housing assistance grant
-- (142G.32, subd. 1(a)); and the duty to report changes by the tenth of the next month (256P.07, subd. 2).
--
-- SEAT: the caregiver who applies for, or receives, MFIP for the family: "Can my family get MFIP? How much will we get each
-- month? When must I report a change?" Duties of the agency and the commissioner are encoded for what they give the family.
--
-- Edition: Minnesota Statutes 2025, chapters 142G and 256P (Office of the Revisor; 142G retrieved 2026-10-19, 256P
-- retrieved 2026-10-24), and the DCYF notice at 51 SR 472 (5 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mn-stat-ch-142G-2025.txt,
-- ../../../minnesota-statutes-chapter-256p-economic-assistance-program-eligibility-and-verification/registers/source-bundle/mn-stat-ch-256P-2025.txt
-- and ../../../minnesota-state-register-mfip-transitional-standard-2026/registers/source-bundle/
-- mn-state-register-51-sr-472-mfip-transitional-standard-2026-10-01.txt. The 2026 session's amendments to 142G (eight
-- provisions, listed in the file's header) are not in the deposited text.
--
-- Inputs, not deposited: which income is earned, unearned or excluded (256P.06), the housing assistance grant as adjusted
-- for the year (142G.32, subd. 1(b)), the unmet-need allocation (142G.33), deemed income (142G.31, subds. 1 to 4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: citizenship, residence and the other conditions of 142G.11 to 142G.15 (asked as one fact); employment
-- services, sanctions and good cause (142G.50 to 142G.71); the diversionary work program; proration in the month of
-- application (142G.32, subd. 1(c)); hardship extensions (142G.42); the split of the payment into cash and food portions.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `MFIP eligibility and assistance payment`

§§ `142G.17, subd. 5 and 51 SR 472 -- the Transitional Standard and the family wage level`

-- 51 SR 472: "The MFIP Transitional Standard and cash and food portions effective October 1, 2026": family size 1, $697; 2,
-- $1,145; 3, $1,470; 4, $1,763; 5, $2,037; 6, $2,364; 7, $2,572; 8, $2,839; 9, $3,103; 10, $3,360; "Over 10", $256 (read
-- as $256 for each person beyond ten: the deposit header says so is unverified; NOTES.md finding 4).
-- 142G.17, subd. 5(a): "based on the number of persons in the assistance unit eligible for both food and cash assistance".
GIVEN `persons eligible for food and cash` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Transitional Standard from October 1, 2026` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 1  THEN 697
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 2  THEN 1145
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 3  THEN 1470
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 4  THEN 1763
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 5  THEN 2037
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 6  THEN 2364
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 7  THEN 2572
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 8  THEN 2839
        IF `persons eligible for food and cash` EQUALS 9  THEN 3103
        OTHERWISE 3360 PLUS 256 TIMES (`persons eligible for food and cash` MINUS 10)

-- 142G.17, subd. 7: "The family wage level is 110 percent of the transitional standard".
GIVEN `transitional standard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family wage level` MEANS 110% TIMES `transitional standard`

@export What are the MFIP Transitional Standard and family wage level for my family from October 1, 2026 (142G.17; 51 SR 472)?
GIVEN `family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people in your MFIP assistance unit are eligible for both food and cash assistance (not counting members on SSI or disqualified)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my MFIP Transitional Standard` MEANS `the Transitional Standard from October 1, 2026` `family size`

§§ `256P.03 -- the earned income disregard`

-- 256P.03, subd. 2: "The agency shall disregard the first $65 of earned income plus one-half of the remaining earned income
-- per month."
GIVEN `gross earned income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earned income disregard` MEANS
    IF `gross earned income` AT MOST 65
    THEN `gross earned income`
    ELSE 65 PLUS 50% TIMES (`gross earned income` MINUS 65)

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

§§ `142G.16, subd. 1 -- the initial income test`

-- (a): "the assistance unit's countable income minus the earned income disregards ... must be below the family wage level";
-- (b): also disregarded: (2) dependent care actually paid, "up to a maximum of $200 per month for each child less than two
-- years of age, and $175 per month for each child two years of age and older"; (3) court-ordered support paid to persons
-- outside the household; (4) the 142G.33 allocation (an input).
GIVEN `gross earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `unearned income` IS A NUMBER
      `dependent care paid` IS A NUMBER
      `children under two in care` IS A NUMBER
      `children two or older in care` IS A NUMBER
      `court-ordered support paid out` IS A NUMBER
      `the 142G.33 allocation` IS A NUMBER
      `family wage level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unit passes the initial income test` IF
    `the counted income` LESS THAN `family wage level`
    WHERE
        `dependent care allowed` MEANS
            `the smaller of` `dependent care paid` ((200 TIMES `children under two in care`) PLUS (175 TIMES `children two or older in care`))
        `the counted income` MEANS
            sum (LIST
                `gross earned income`,
                0 MINUS `the earned income disregard` `gross earned income`,
                0 MINUS `dependent care allowed`,
                `unearned income`,
                0 MINUS `court-ordered support paid out`,
                0 MINUS `the 142G.33 allocation`)

§§ `142G.16, subd. 2; 142G.31, subd. 6; 142G.32 -- the monthly assistance payment`

-- 142G.16, subd. 2: "(a) Apply an income disregard ... to gross earnings and subtract this amount from the family wage
-- level. If the difference is equal to or greater than the MFIP transitional standard, the assistance payment is equal to
-- the MFIP transitional standard. If the difference is less ..., the assistance payment is equal to the difference." (The
-- text says "subtract this amount", meaning the earnings after the disregard: NOTES.md finding 1.) "(d) Subtract unearned
-- income dollar for dollar"; "(e) ... first treating gross earned income as specified in paragraph (a) ... unearned income
-- must be subtracted from that amount". "To be eligible for MFIP, the result ... must be at least $1."
-- 142G.31, subd. 6: "$50 of the value of public and assisted rental subsidies provided through ... HUD" counts as unearned
-- income (the full subsidy if under $50), unless a participant is 60 or older, a caregiver is certified ill or
-- incapacitated, or needed at home, for more than 30 days, or the parental caregiver is on SSI.
-- 142G.32, subd. 1(a): "an MFIP housing assistance grant of $110 per month, unless" the unit has a HUD subsidy subject to
-- 142G.31, subd. 6, or is a child-only case; (b): adjusted each October 1 (the adjusted figure is an input).
DECLARE `My monthly MFIP` IS ONE OF
    `an assistance payment of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER, `housing assistance grant` IS A NUMBER
    `not eligible: the result of 142G.16, subd. 2 is less than $1`

GIVEN `transitional standard` IS A NUMBER
      `gross earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `unearned income` IS A NUMBER
      `court-ordered support paid out` IS A NUMBER
      `the 142G.33 allocation` IS A NUMBER
      `HUD rental subsidy` IS A NUMBER
      `the HUD subsidy rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `child-only case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `housing assistance grant for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `My monthly MFIP`
`the 142G.16, subd. 2 payment` MEANS
    IF `the result` LESS THAN 1
    THEN `not eligible: the result of 142G.16, subd. 2 is less than $1`
    ELSE `an assistance payment of` `the result` `the housing grant`
    WHERE
        `counted earnings` MEANS (`gross earned income` MINUS `the earned income disregard` `gross earned income`) MINUS `court-ordered support paid out`
        `the difference` MEANS (`the family wage level` `transitional standard`) MINUS `counted earnings`
        `after earnings` MEANS `the smaller of` `the difference` `transitional standard`
        `subsidy counted` MEANS
            IF `HUD rental subsidy` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the HUD subsidy rule applies`
            THEN `the smaller of` 50 `HUD rental subsidy`
            ELSE 0
        -- The 142G.33 allocation reduces the income counted (subd. 2(c)); the text does not say against which income, so it
        -- is added back to the result, which 142G.17, subd. 7 caps at the transitional standard (NOTES.md finding 2).
        `the result` MEANS `the smaller of` `transitional standard` (((`after earnings` MINUS `unearned income`) MINUS `subsidy counted`) PLUS `the 142G.33 allocation`)
        `the housing grant` MEANS
            IF (`HUD rental subsidy` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the HUD subsidy rule applies`) OR `child-only case`
            THEN 0
            ELSE `housing assistance grant for the year`

§§ `142G.10, 256P.02, 142G.40 -- other conditions`

-- 256P.02, subd. 2: the equity value of the unit's cash, bank accounts, liquid stocks and bonds, vehicles beyond one per
-- member aged 16 or over, and business accounts used for non-business expenses "must not exceed $10,000".
-- 142G.40, subd. 1(a): a unit "in which any adult caregiver has received 60 months of cash assistance funded in whole or in
-- part by the TANF block grant ... is ineligible"; subd. 4(a): months when the caregiver is 60 or older do not count (the
-- count is asked net of the exempt months of subds. 2 to 4).
DECLARE `Can my family get MFIP` IS ONE OF
    `yes, with` HAS `the payment` IS A `My monthly MFIP`
    `no: the family must include a minor child living with a caregiver, or be a pregnant woman and her spouse (142G.17, subd. 1)`
    `no: the general eligibility requirements of 142G.11 to 142G.15 must be met (142G.10, subd. 1)`
    `no: the unit's countable personal property is over $10,000 (256P.02, subd. 2)`
    `no: an adult caregiver has received 60 counted months of TANF-funded cash assistance (142G.40, subd. 1)`
    `no: countable income after the disregards is not below the family wage level (142G.16, subd. 1)`

@export Can my family get MFIP, and how much will the monthly assistance payment be (from October 1, 2026)?
GIVEN `minor child or pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family has a child under 18 living with you as caregiver, or you are a pregnant woman (with your spouse, if any)
      `general conditions met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every member meets the citizenship or immigration, Minnesota residence and other conditions of sections 142G.11 to 142G.15
      `property value` IS A NUMBER @desc The equity value of your unit's cash, bank accounts, readily available stocks and bonds, extra vehicles (beyond one per member aged 16 or over) and business accounts used for personal expenses, in US dollars
      `months of TANF cash` IS A NUMBER @desc The most months of TANF-funded cash assistance (MFIP or another state's) any adult caregiver in your unit has received, not counting exempt months (for example months when the caregiver was 60 or older)
      `family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people in your MFIP unit are eligible for both food and cash assistance
      `gross earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit's gross earned income for the month, in US dollars
      `unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The unit's countable unearned income for the month (for example child support received, unemployment benefits, Social Security), after the costs of getting it, in US dollars
      `dependent care paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay a month for the care of children while you work, in US dollars
      `children under 2 in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those children are under 2
      `children 2 or older in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those children are 2 or older
      `support paid out` IS A NUMBER @desc Court-ordered child or spousal support you pay to people outside your household each month, in US dollars
      `unmet need allocation` IS A NUMBER @desc The allocation under 142G.33 for an ineligible spouse or child under 21 you support who lives with you, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `HUD subsidy` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly value of any public or assisted rental subsidy from HUD that your household gets, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `subsidy exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member is 60 or older, a caregiver is certified ill or incapacitated or needed at home for more than 30 days, or the parent caregiver gets SSI (then the subsidy is not counted)
      `child-only case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your case is child-only (the caregiver is not in the assistance unit)
      `housing grant` IS A NUMBER @desc The MFIP housing assistance grant for the year as adjusted by the commissioner ($110 before adjustment), in US dollars
GIVETH A `Can my family get MFIP`
`Can my family get MFIP` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `minor child or pregnancy`) THEN `no: the family must include a minor child living with a caregiver, or be a pregnant woman and her spouse (142G.17, subd. 1)`
        IF (NOT `general conditions met`) THEN `no: the general eligibility requirements of 142G.11 to 142G.15 must be met (142G.10, subd. 1)`
        IF `property value` GREATER THAN 10000 THEN `no: the unit's countable personal property is over $10,000 (256P.02, subd. 2)`
        IF `months of TANF cash` AT LEAST 60 THEN `no: an adult caregiver has received 60 counted months of TANF-funded cash assistance (142G.40, subd. 1)`
        IF (NOT (`the unit passes the initial income test` `gross earnings` `unearned income` `dependent care paid` `children under 2 in care` `children 2 or older in care` `support paid out` `unmet need allocation` (`the family wage level` `TS`)))
            THEN `no: countable income after the disregards is not below the family wage level (142G.16, subd. 1)`
        OTHERWISE `yes, with` (`the 142G.16, subd. 2 payment` `TS` `gross earnings` `unearned income` `support paid out` `unmet need allocation` `HUD subsidy` (NOT `subsidy exception`) `child-only case` `housing grant`)
    WHERE
        `TS` MEANS `the Transitional Standard from October 1, 2026` `family size`

@export How much of my monthly earnings does MFIP disregard (256P.03)?
GIVEN `gross earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross earned income for the month, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my earnings is disregarded` MEANS `the earned income disregard` `gross earnings`

§§ `256P.07, subd. 2 -- reporting a change (only once something has changed)`

-- "An applicant or assistance unit must report changes that affect eligibility or benefits ... during the application
-- period or by the tenth of the month following the month that the assistance unit's circumstances changed." Counted in
-- days from the first day of the month after the change (day 0 = the 1st, so the 10th is day 9).
DECLARE `MFIP party` IS ONE OF `the assistance unit`
DECLARE `MFIP act` IS ONE OF `report the change to the agency`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `MFIP party` `MFIP act`
`256P.07, subd. 2 -- report a change by the tenth of the following month` MEANS
    PARTY  `the assistance unit`
    MUST   `report the change to the agency`
    WITHIN 9
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the assistance unit` BECAUSE "a change affecting eligibility or benefits not reported by the tenth of the following month (256P.07, subd. 2)"

@export By what day of the month after a change must my MFIP unit report it (256P.07, subd. 2)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`By what day of the next month must I report a change` MEANS 10
